.TH "DOCUMENT.POINTERLOCKERROR_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Document.pointerlockerror_event \- Document: pointerlockerror event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]pointerlockerror\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when locking
the pointer failed (for technical reasons or because the permission was
denied).
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqpointerlockerror\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onpointerlockerror = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Using \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] para = document.querySelector(\(dqp\(dq);

document.addEventListener(\(dqpointerlockerror\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqError locking pointer\(dq);
});
.EE
.PP
Using the \f[CR]onpointerlockerror\f[R] event handler property (but note
that this replaces other event listeners added using
\f[CR]onpointerlockerror\f[R], if any):
.IP
.EX
document.onpointerlockerror = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqError locking pointer\(dq);
};
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Using Pointer Lock API
